**3. Branching Strategy (GitFlow)**

```bash
# Branch naming
# feature/TICKET-description
# bugfix/TICKET-description
# hotfix/TICKET-description
# release/v1.2.3

# Start feature
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop
git checkout -b feature/ABC-123-user-authentication

# Work on feature
git add .
git commit -m "feat(auth): add login endpoint"

# Update from develop
git fetch origin
git rebase origin/develop

# Finish feature
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop
git merge --no-ff feature/ABC-123-user-authentication
git branch -d feature/ABC-123-user-authentication
git push origin develop

# Create release
git checkout -b release/v1.2.0 develop
# ... prepare release ...
git checkout main
git merge --no-ff release/v1.2.0
git tag -a v1.2.0 -m "Release v1.2.0"
git push origin main --tags

# Hotfix
git checkout -b hotfix/ABC-456-fix-bug main
# ... fix ...
git checkout main
git merge --no-ff hotfix/ABC-456-fix-bug
git tag -a v1.2.1 -m "Hotfix v1.2.1"
git push origin main --tags
```

**4. Commit Convention**

```bash
# Format
# <type>(<scope>): <description>
#
# [optional body]
#
# [optional footer(s)]

# Types
# feat:     New feature
# fix:      Bug fix
# docs:     Documentation
# style:    Formatting, missing semicolons, etc
# refactor: Code refactoring
# test:     Adding tests
# chore:    Maintenance tasks
# perf:     Performance improvements
# ci:       CI/CD changes
# build:    Build system changes
# revert:   Revert commits

# Examples
git commit -m "feat(auth): add JWT token validation"
git commit -m "fix(api): handle null pointer in user endpoint"
git commit -m "docs(readme): update installation instructions"
git commit -m "refactor(users): extract user validation to service"
git commit -m "test(checkout): add integration tests for payment flow"
git commit -m "perf(api): optimize database queries for user list"

# With body
git commit -m "feat(payments): add Stripe integration
- Add Stripe SDK for payment processing
- Implement webhook handling for payment events
- Add retry logic for failed payments"

# Breaking changes
git commit -m "feat(api): change response format for /users
BREAKING CHANGE: /users now returns array instead of object"
```

