### 3. Merging Strategies

```bash
# Merge strategy for feature branches
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop
git merge --no-ff feature/PROJ-123-user-auth

# No fast-forward to preserve branch history
# --no-ff creates a merge commit even for fast-forward

# Rebase before merge (cleaner history)
git checkout feature/PROJ-123-user-auth
git fetch origin
git rebase origin/develop

# Resolve conflicts
# Edit conflicting files
git add .
git rebase --continue

# After rebase, force push
git push --force-with-lease

# Hotfix workflow
git checkout main
git pull
git checkout -b hotfix/PROJ-200-security
# Make changes
git commit -m "fix(security): patch vulnerability"
git checkout main
git merge --no-ff hotfix/PROJ-200-security
git tag v1.0.1
git push origin main --tags
git push origin hotfix/PROJ-200-security  # For merge to develop
```

