### 6. Hotfix Workflow Example

```bash
# Critical bug in production
git checkout main
git pull origin main
git checkout -b hotfix/PROJ-200-critical-bug

# Implement fix
git add src/
git commit -m "fix: resolve critical data race condition"

# Test locally
npm run test
npm run test:integration

# Push and create PR
git push -u origin hotfix/PROJ-200-critical-bug

# After review, merge to main
git checkout main
git pull origin main
git merge --no-ff hotfix/PROJ-200-critical-bug

# Tag the release
git tag -a v1.0.1 -m "Hotfix: resolve critical bug PROJ-200"
git push origin main --tags

# Merge to develop
git checkout develop
git merge --no-ff hotfix/PROJ-200-critical-bug
git push origin develop

# Clean up
git branch -d hotfix/PROJ-200-critical-bug
```

### 7. Release Workflow Example

```bash
# Prepare release
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop
git checkout -b release/v1.1.0

# Update version
npm version minor --no-git-tag-version
git add package.json
git commit -m "chore: bump version to 1.1.0"

# Run release tests
npm run test
npm run test:integration
npm run test:e2e

# If issues found
git commit -m "fix(release): resolve test failures"
git push

# Merge to main
git checkout main
git pull origin main
git merge --no-ff release/v1.1.0

# Tag release
git tag -a v1.1.0 -m "Release version 1.1.0"
git push origin main --tags

# Merge back to develop
git checkout develop
git merge --no-ff release/v1.1.0
git push origin develop

# Clean up
git branch -d release/v1.1.0
```

### 8. Tagging Strategy

```bash
# Semantic versioning tags
# v<major>.<minor>.<patch>

# Create lightweight tag
git tag v1.0.0

# Create annotated tag (recommended)
git tag -a v1.0.0 -m "Release version 1.0.0"

# Create tag with signature
git tag -s v1.0.0 -m "Release version 1.0.0"

# Tag after commit
git tag -a v1.0.0 <commit-sha>

# Push tags
git push origin v1.0.0
git push origin --tags

# List tags
git tag -l
git tag -l "v1.*"

# Delete tags
git tag -d v1.0.0           # Local
git push origin :refs/tags/v1.0.0  # Remote
```

