## Worktree Workflow (from Superpowers)

> **Source:** [obra/superpowers](https://github.com/obra/superpowers) `using-git-worktrees` + `finishing-a-development-branch` skills (248k stars) — "Creates isolated workspace on new branch, runs project setup, verifies clean test baseline."

### When to Use a Worktree

Use a worktree when:
- Working on a feature that takes more than one session
- Comparing two branches side-by-side without stashing
- Running long-lived dev servers (different ports per worktree)
- Reviewing a PR locally without disrupting the main checkout

### Create a Worktree

```bash
# From main checkout, add a worktree for the new feature branch
git worktree add ../proj-feature-auth feature/PROJ-123-user-auth

# That gives you a sibling directory at ../proj-feature-auth
# already on branch feature/PROJ-123-user-auth
cd ../proj-feature-auth
npm install   # or whatever setup the project has
npm test      # verify clean baseline BEFORE writing code
```

A worktree shares the same `.git` database with the main checkout. There's no remote push until you decide to ship.

### Daily Use

```bash
# Inside the worktree, work normally
git add . && git commit -m "feat(auth): add login form"

# Inspect a different branch from the main checkout, NOT from this worktree
cd ../proj-main
git fetch origin
git checkout origin/feature/PROJ-456-other-stuff   # bonus worktree, auto-managed

# Back to your work
cd ../proj-feature-auth
```

### Finishing a Development Branch

When tasks are complete and all tests pass, present options to the user:

| Option | When to pick |
|---|---|
| **Merge** (no-ff) | Branch is small, single-purpose, ready to integrate |
| **Open PR** | Need code review or CI checks before merge |
| **Keep** (don't integrate yet) | Branch is WIP, dependencies not ready, want to return |
| **Discard** | Branch was a dead end, throw away the worktree + branch |

Cleanup script for the discard path:

```bash
# Inside main checkout, remove the worktree and the branch
git worktree remove ../proj-feature-auth
git branch -D feature/PROJ-123-user-auth
```

For Merge / PR / Keep, run project test suite one last time, then follow the existing §Release Workflow in this file.
